title: The <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> leaves the Popular Front government[? if in_popular_front_heartland and not in_popular_front:&nbsp;in Heartland?]!
subtitle: As expected.
new-page: true
on-arrival: lvp_relation -= 6; lvp_right += 3 {! 
if (Q.lvp_formed) {
    Q.popular_front_coalition = parseFloat((Q.marcher_r + Q.collectivist_r + Q.unionist_r - Q.bvp_r + Q.sapd_r).toFixed(1));
} else if (Q.liberal_parliament == 0 && Q.bourgeois_parliament_ddp == 0) {
    Q.popular_front_coalition = parseFloat((Q.marcher_r + Q.collectivist_r + Q.unionist_r + Q.ddp_r - Q.bvp_r + Q.sapd_r).toFixed(1));
} else if (Q.liberal_parliament == 1 || Q.bourgeois_parliament_ddp == 1) {
    Q.popular_front_coalition = parseFloat((Q.marcher_r + Q.collectivist_r + Q.unionist_r - Q.bvp_r + Q.sapd_r).toFixed(1));
}

if (Q.lvp_formed) {
    Q.popular_front_coalition_heartland = parseFloat((Q.marcher_r_heartland + Q.collectivist_r_heartland + Q.unionist_r_heartland + Q.sapd_r_heartland).toFixed(1));
} else if (Q.liberal_parliament == 0) {
    Q.popular_front_coalition_heartland = parseFloat((Q.marcher_r_heartland + Q.collectivist_r_heartland + Q.unionist_r_heartland + Q.ddp_r_heartland + Q.sapd_r_heartland).toFixed(1));
} else if (Q.liberal_parliament == 1) {
    Q.popular_front_coalition_heartland = parseFloat((Q.marcher_r_heartland + Q.collectivist_r_heartland + Q.unionist_r_heartland + Q.sapd_r_heartland).toFixed(1));
}
!}
view-if: ((in_popular_front and ddp_in_popular_front) or (in_popular_front_heartland and ddp_in_popular_front_heartland)) and lvp_formed 
tags: event

= The <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> leaves the Popular Front government!

With the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> dissolving itself and joining with the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> in a significantly more right-wing party, they have expectedly withdrawn their support of our incumbent Popular Front[? if in_popular_front_heartland and not in_popular_front:&nbsp;in Heartland?][? if in_popular_front_heartland and in_popular_front:&nbsp;in Heartland, and nationally?]. 

[? if in_popular_front: [? if popular_front_coalition >= 50: Fortunately, we still possess a majority without their votes, and they are able to leave government without causing much of a ruckus. ?][? if popular_front_coalition < 50: Unfortunately, the former <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>'s votes was key for the survival of the Popular Front, and now our government lacks a majority without them. [? if constructive_vonc: We can continue on as a minority government however due to our constitutional reforms. ?]?] ?]

[? if in_popular_front_heartland: [? if popular_front_coalition_heartland >= 50: In Heartland, we luckily possess a majority without their votes, and they are able to leave the state government while we still govern with the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?]. ?][? if popular_front_coalition_heartland < 50: In Heartland, the former <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>'s votes was key for the survival of its Popular Front, and now our government lacks a majority without them. ?] ?]

- @popular_front_lives: Ok then.
- @collapse: Our government faces a vote of no confidence!
- @collapse_prussia: Our Heartland government faces a vote of no confidence!

@popular_front_lives
view-if: ((popular_front_coalition >= 50 or not ddp_in_popular_front or constructive_vonc) and (popular_front_coalition_heartland >= 50 or not ddp_in_popular_front_heartland)) and not (popular_front_coalition >= 50 and popular_front_coalition_heartland < 50 and ddp_in_popular_front_heartland)
on-arrival: ddp_in_popular_front = 0; ddp_in_popular_front_heartland = 0

Their former cabinet positions [? if in_popular_front and in_popular_front_heartland: nationally and in Heartland?][? if not in_popular_front and in_popular_front_heartland: in Heartland?] (if they had any) have been transferred to the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?].

@collapse
view-if: popular_front_coalition < 50 and ddp_in_popular_front and not constructive_vonc
on-arrival: time_to_election = 3; marcher_in_government = 0; grand_coalition_collapsed = 1 if in_grand_coalition; in_grand_coalition = 0; in_weimar_coalition = 0; in_popular_front = 0; ddp_in_popular_front = 0; marcher_toleration = 0; marcher_toleration_right = 0; foreign_minister_party = "Gold"; foreign_minister_party = "LVP" if lvp_formed; interior_minister_party = "Unionist"; justice_minister_party = "I"; labor_minister_party = "Unionist"; army_minister_party = "I"; economic_minister_party = ddp_name; economic_minister_party = "LVP" if lvp_formed; finance_minister_party = "Gold"; finance_minister_party = "LVP" if lvp_formed; agriculture_minister_party = "Unionist"; labor_minister = "Sedgewick"; interior_minister = "Werth"; finance_minister = "Moldenhauer"; economic_minister = "Curtius"; justice_minister = "Koch-Weser"; foreign_minister = "Stratton" if not stresemann_dead; foreign_minister = "Curtius" if stresemann_dead; agriculture_minister = "Dietrich"; army_minister = "Ravabelle"; coalition_dissent = 0; pro_republic -= 4; guild_marcher -= 3; burgher_marcher -= 2; commons_marcher -= 3 if pro_republic < 50; commons_marcher -= 4 if pro_republic < 40; guild_royalist += 4 if pro_republic < 50; burgher_royalist += 3 if pro_republic < 50
go-to: let_it_happen_hindenburg if president_ideology != "Left"; let_it_happen_braun if president_ideology == "Left"

@let_it_happen_hindenburg
on-arrival: chancellor = "Askew"; chancellor_party = "Unionist"; welfare -= 2; bruning_event_timer = 6 if not bruning_event_seen and year >= 1930
go-to: elections if bruning_event_seen or year < 1930

The vote succeeds with [+ 100 - popular_front_coalition +]% of the vote, and our government has resigned. Chancellor Askew has been appointed as the head of a new cabinet, consisting solely of the propertied parties. He immediately proceeds to cut welfare spending substantially.

[? if not bruning_event_seen and year >= 1930: New elections haven't been called yet but it's likely that they will be soon, considering Askew most likely doesn't have the majority of the Assembly behind him. ?]

@elections
call: set_next_election_time
go-to: collapse_prussia if (popular_front_coalition_heartland < 50 and ddp_in_popular_front_heartland)

New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].

@let_it_happen_braun
on-arrival: marcher_caretaker = 1
call: set_next_election_time
go-to: collapse_prussia if (popular_front_coalition_heartland < 50 and ddp_in_popular_front_heartland)

The vote succeeds, and our government has resigned. Chancellor [+ chancellor +] remains as the head of a caretaker government, but no longer has the power to enact new policies.

New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].

@collapse_prussia
view-if: (popular_front_coalition_heartland < 50 and ddp_in_popular_front_heartland) and not (in_popular_front and ddp_in_popular_front and popular_front_coalition < 50 and not constructive_vonc)
on-arrival: was_in_social_catholic_coalition_heartland = 0; was_in_social_liberal_coalition_heartland = 0; was_in_weimar_coalition_heartland = 0; was_in_grand_coalition_heartland = 0; was_in_social_catholic_coalition_heartland = 1 if in_social_catholic_coalition_heartland == 1 or in_minority_social_catholic_coalition_heartland == 1; was_in_social_liberal_coalition_heartland = 1 if in_social_liberal_coalition_heartland == 1 or in_minority_social_liberal_coalition_heartland == 1; was_in_weimar_coalition_heartland = 1 if ((in_weimar_coalition_heartland == 1 or in_minority_weimar_coalition_heartland == 1) or (in_grand_coalition_heartland == 1 and lvp_formed)); was_in_grand_coalition_heartland = 1 if (in_grand_coalition_heartland == 1 or in_minority_grand_coalition_heartland == 1); in_right_coalition_heartland = 0; in_social_catholic_coalition_heartland = 0; in_social_liberal_coalition_heartland = 0; in_weimar_coalition_heartland = 0; in_grand_coalition_heartland = 0; in_minority_grand_coalition_heartland = 0; in_popular_front_heartland = 0; in_left_front_heartland = 0; in_marcher_majority_heartland = 0; in_center_right_coalition_heartland = 0; in_far_right_coalition_heartland = 0; in_minority_weimar_coalition_heartland = 0; in_minority_social_catholic_coalition_heartland = 0; in_minority_social_liberal_coalition_heartland = 0; marcher_heartland = 0; right_heartland = 0; ddp_in_popular_front_heartland = 0; collectivist_goals_seen_heartland = 0; marcher_toleration_heartland = 0
call: set_next_election_time_prussia

New Heartland elections have been set for [+ next_election_month_heartland : month +] [+ next_election_year_heartland +]. 
